id: pm-j1r8gl
title: "pm activity answers what happened to one item in the last half hour when the agent asked what changed in the workspace: 20 rows cover 5 of the 272 items touched in 24 hours and none carries a title"
description: "Measured on the live tracker: the default bound is 20 rows over an unfiltered reverse-chronological merge of all 2443 history streams. Those 20 rows resolve to 5 distinct items spanning 27 minutes, while 757 events across 272 distinct items landed in the preceding 24 hours - so the default names 1.8 percent of the items touched in a day. Rows carry id, op, ts and author only, so rebuilding context costs one pm get per id, and 18 of the 20 carry no message at all. The op vocabulary is dominated by mechanical sub-mutations: update 25.1 percent, comment_add 18.8, files_add 15.4, tests_add 7.1, claim 6.4, release 5.4 - more than half the window is attachment and lock churn rather than lifecycle change, and the lock verb release reads as a version release. An item-centric digest over a time window (one row per item touched, carrying type, status, event count, last timestamp, a bounded op summary and the title) covers 15 items in 2426 bytes against the current 2918 bytes for 5. The join is already paid for: prepareActivityHistoryRead already reads every item light metadata record to enforce the history-stream policy and then discards everything except the ids."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: activity,agent-ux,context-efficiency,history,output-contracts,token-budget
created_at: "2026-08-11T05:24:00.618Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T05:26:15.172Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Default pm activity returns one row per item touched inside a declared time window, carrying id, type, status, event count, first and last timestamp, a bounded op summary and the title, ordered by recency or event count; The envelope declares the window plus event, item and author totals and a bounded op histogram, so an agent can distinguish a quiet period from a truncated one; The raw per-event stream stays reachable behind an explicit flag with the compact row shape unchanged, and --full, --provenance and the existing filters are unaffected; Item metadata is joined from the light metadata read the command already performs, adding no second traversal, and the digest cost is asserted by the token-budget-gate corpus; Contracts snapshot, completion scripts, MCP surface and docs are regenerated in the same change"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
